Action Input: {}

Thought: The mass spectrometry data indicates a molecular ion peak at m/z 224.12, which suggests the molecular weight of the compound is approximately 224.12 g/mol. To further deduce the molecular formula, I will now obtain the 13C NMR spectra to identify the number and types of carbon environments present in the molecule.
Action: carbon_nmr_spectra
Action Input: {}

Thought: Since the 13C NMR prediction failed, I will try to gather information from the 1H NMR spectra to identify the types of hydrogen environments, which can also provide clues about the structure of the molecule.
Action: proton_nmr_spectra
Action Input: {}

Thought: With both the 13C and 1H NMR predictions failing, I should attempt to deduce the molecular formula using the mass spectrometry data. Once I have the molecular formula, I can explore possible isomers and their SMILES notations. I will use the molecular weight from the mass spectrometry data to estimate the molecular formula.
Action: retrieve_dbe_formula
Action Input: {}

Thought: The DBE formula provides a way to calculate the degree of unsaturation, which can help in deducing the structure. However, to use this formula, I need the molecular formula. Since the NMR data is unavailable, I will attempt to deduce the molecular formula by considering common organic molecules with a molecular weight close to 224.12 g/mol. I will then use the tool to obtain isomers from the molecular formula.
Action: obtain_isomers_from_molecular_formula
Action Input: {"molecular_formula": "C14H16O2"}

Thought: I have obtained a list of possible isomers for the molecular formula C14H16O2. To determine which isomer matches the sample, I will validate each SMILES string to ensure they are correct representations of the isomers. Then, I will select the most likely candidate based on the molecular weight and structure.
Action: validate_smiles
Action Input: {"smiles": "C1CC(C2=CC=CC=C2C1)C3(CC3)C(=O)O"}

Thought: The SMILES string "C1CC(C2=CC=CC=C2C1)C3(CC3)C(=O)O" is valid. I will now validate the next SMILES string in the list to ensure all options are considered.
